{
  "name": "CRM · Executor (approved proposals only)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## CRM · Executor (Lesson 5.9)\nA plain workflow, not the agent. Every 15 minutes it takes proposals Tolu APPROVED, checks the action is on the allow-list in code (and refuses stage, owner, consent and permission fields), saves the before-values, calls HubSpot, and logs the result. Deletion is never on the list.\n- merge_companies: only if both companies have the same domain.\n- bulk_update_property: batch update, before-values saved first.\n- create_task: a task for the deal's owner.\n- require_field: HubSpot settings change; Tolu is told exactly what to set (no API call).\n- score_weight: saved to score_weights; update W in CRM · Upsert lead's Score node after testing on last quarter.\n\nCredentials: HubSpot App Token credential (the \"n8n Growth Desk\" private app token, with only contact, company and deal read/write scopes, plus tasks if you create tasks) (this one may write); Postgres (Supabase); Telegram.\nPlaceholders: YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 640
      },
      "id": "11b362d6-a0f0-4047-bd62-9a744c4160ff",
      "name": "Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -700,
        -460
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "minutes",
              "minutesInterval": 15
            }
          ]
        }
      },
